{
  "title": "quiet_check can hang after failed parallel targets",
  "description": "The quiet `make check` wrapper in `scripts/checks/quiet_check.py` can stall after it has already printed some parallel target results, leaving the operator without the failing target logs or a final exit.\n\
\n\
Observed on 2026-03-21 while fixing `p4-burn-down-ruff-unused-argument-ignores`:\n\
- `make check` printed `format-check FAIL`, later `verify-decks ok`, `test FAIL`, and `typecheck ok`\n\
- after the child `pytest` and `mypy` processes exited, the wrapper still did not print the collected failure output or return\n\
- interrupting it showed the main thread still blocked in `for future in as_completed(futures)`\n\
\n\
This makes failed checks substantially slower to diagnose because you have to fall back to manual subtarget runs to recover the actual failure details.\n\
\n\
Relevant files:\n\
- `scripts/checks/quiet_check.py`\n\
- `Makefile`",
